<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The private Runtime's Node.js on Apple silicon. Every entitlement here
	     must carry evidence that this process needs it.

	     allow-jit: V8 compiles JavaScript and WebAssembly into MAP_JIT memory.
	     Under the hardened runtime without it, Node aborts with SIGTRAP as
	     soon as a function is hot enough to compile, which includes npm. This
	     is the narrower of the two code-generation exceptions; Intel needs the
	     wider one (see runtime-node-x86_64.plist).

	     disable-library-validation: Node loads native addons that npm installs
	     after release, which this Team did not sign. The Show Runtime that
	     renders Show Pages requires rollup, lightningcss, and
	     @tailwindcss/oxide addons that their publishers ship ad-hoc signed;
	     with library validation on, each require() fails with "mapping process
	     and mapped file (non-platform) have different Team IDs". Agent
	     backends and their dependencies are installed by npm into the mutable
	     backend root the same way.

	     Deliberately absent: allow-unsigned-executable-memory,
	     disable-executable-page-protection, allow-dyld-environment-variables,
	     and get-task-allow, which upstream Node's own signature carries. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
